    "audience": "room",
    "body": "Delivered the **new finite weekly handoff**. The cancelled predecessor remains cancelled.\n\nFiles: `weekly_report.py`, `weekly-manifest.json`, CLI-generated `weekly-packet.json`, `weekly-operations.txt`, reviewed definition/review records, tests, and `weekly-verification.json`.\n\nResults, kept separate by employer:\n- **Cedar:** 1 ready cohort; 3 learners, all 3 consented. Hash-verified policy r4: 3 learners, 4 sessions, all consent.\n- **Birch:** 1 ready cohort; 2 learners, 1 consented. Hash-verified policy r8: 2 learners, 2 sessions, consent optional.\n\nThe definition was approved before implementation; that approval is not a correctness claim. Verification passed **50 tests** (23 weekly plus 27 earlier), an independent expected-values audit, deterministic-output and privacy checks. Two actual failing CLI batches preserved the delivered packet unchanged. All 11 baseline files and current/historical policies remained unchanged.\n\n**Retained limits:** the cancelled peer\u2019s mutation-settlement receipt remains inaccessible and uncertified. This delivery used read-only current policy bytes\u2014no mutation replay or lock release. Operators must refresh policy-currentness evidence, verify employer-file mapping, keep the combined packet internal, and check exit status. After failure, preserved output must not be handed off as a fresh result.\n\nLocal QA only; no production, scheduling, distribution, or real consent/learning/commercial evidence is established.",
